  "nl_text": "The database schema named 'rschema_0473' contains four tables: 'Publication', 'Customer', 'Administrator', and 'Order'.\nThe 'Publication' table represents the published books and their details. It has columns for 'Author' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Price' (a floating-point number), 'Publication_ID' (an integer primary key), 'Title' (a string of up to 255 characters), and 'Type' (a string of up to 255 characters).\nThe 'Customer' table represents the customers who can place orders. It has columns for 'Customer_ID' (an integer primary key), 'Email' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Name' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Password' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Phone' (a string of up to 255 characters), and 'Registration_Status' (a string of up to 255 characters).\nThe 'Administrator' table represents the administrators who manage the system. It has columns for 'Administrator_ID' (an integer primary key), 'Email' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Name' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Password' (a string of up to 255 characters), and 'Phone' (a string of up to 255 characters).\nThe 'Order' table represents the orders placed by customers. It has columns for 'Customer_ID' (an integer that references 'Customer_ID' in the 'Customer' table), 'Order_Status' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Order_Time' (a datetime), 'Payment_Method' (a string of up to 255 characters), 'Publication_ID' (an integer that references 'Publication_ID' in the 'Publication' table), and 'Shipping_Address' (a string of up to 255 characters). The primary key of this table is a composite of 'Customer_ID', 'Publication_ID', and 'Order_Time'. The 'Customer_ID' and 'Publication_ID' columns are foreign keys that reference the 'Customer' and 'Publication' tables respectively.",
  "gold_question": "A publishing house plans to develop an online store, ACShop, for selling academic publications. The functional requirements are as follows: The online academic publications include papers, academic reports, and lecture materials. Publication information includes Publication ID, Title, Author, Price, and Type. Customer information includes Customer ID, Name, Phone, Email, Password, and Registration Status. ACShop will automatically generate orders, with order information including Publication ID, Customer ID, Shipping Address, Payment Method, Order Status, and Order Time. Administrators are responsible for maintaining the online publication catalog, including adding new publications or updating information on available publications. Administrator information includes Administrator ID, Name, Phone, Email, and Password.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_deepseek/0473.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0473\nCREATE TABLE `Publication` (\n  `Publication_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Author` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Price` float NOT NULL,\n  `Type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Publication_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Customer` (\n  `Customer_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Phone` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Registration_Status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Customer_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Administrator` (\n  `Administrator_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Password` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Phone` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Administrator_ID`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `Order` (\n  `Customer_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Publication_ID` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `Order_Time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `Order_Status` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Payment_Method` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `Shipping_Address` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`Customer_ID`, `Publication_ID`, `Order_Time`),\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`Customer_ID`) REFERENCES `Customer` (`Customer_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `order_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`Publication_ID`) REFERENCES `Publication` (`Publication_ID`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
